cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ManuVox: Auditing the Train–Serve Gap of a Landmark-Based Sign Recognizer on a Laptop"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Shukla
    given-names: Swapnil
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, India
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Swapnil007-Curious/ManuVox"
url: "https://swapnil007-curious.github.io/ManuVox/"
abstract: >-
  ManuVox (research codename Edge-Vision) is an in-browser recognizer of 250 isolated American
  Sign Language signs from MediaPipe landmarks that runs on a low-power laptop, together with the
  code, configurations and result files of a measurement study of its train–serve gap.
keywords:
  - sign language recognition
  - American Sign Language
  - MediaPipe
  - train-serve skew
  - on-device inference
  - onnxruntime-web
